<title>GREECE: CLOSED-END FUND ORION GOES EX-DIV AUG 20.</title>
<headline>CLOSED-END FUND ORION GOES EX-DIV AUG 20.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Closed-end fund Orion said it will distribute an interim dividend of 50 drachmas a share for the first half of the year. Dividend payments will start August 20.</p>
<p>On the same date, Orion shares will trade ex-dividend, without coupon number two.</p>
<p>First half profit rose to 180.9 million drachmas from 23 million in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
